# QMD Integration Module (DE5 Adaptive Phase Engine)

This module provides a **Quantum Motor Dynamics (QMD)** extension for OpenESC firmware.  
It implements the **DE5 real-time torque proxy** and an **adaptive phase-tracking loop** that enhance BLDC/PMSM performance through improved phase alignment and torque estimation — entirely in firmware.

---

## 🔧 Features

- **RT Proxy Torque Estimator**  
  Algebraic DE5-based formulation replacing traditional cosine-phase dependence for electromagnetic torque.  
  Works as a continuous estimator of the instantaneous torque component.

- **Adaptive Phase Controller**  
  Non-blocking PI loop that continuously adjusts the electrical phase offset to maximize the RT proxy value.  
  Operates in real time within the main FOC loop.

- **Active Probe (Optional)**  
  Hill-climb routine with micro-perturbations in phase (`±probe_delta_rad`) to empirically locate the optimal torque phase.  
  Runs asynchronously — no blocking delays or PWM interference.

- **CAN Interface**  
  Two CAN message IDs:
  - `0x320`: Command (mode control, gain update, parameter select)  
  - `0x321`: Telemetry (RT proxy, phase offset)

- **Modes of Operation**
  | Mode | Description |
  |------|--------------|
  | `IDLE` | Module disabled |
  | `OBSERVE` | Passive monitoring |
  | `PROBE` | Active phase probing |
  | `ADAPT` | Continuous adaptive loop |
  | `LOCKED` | Hold last optimized phase |

