🧩 Implementation Notes
    • The QMD module does not replace OpenESC’s FOC — it augments it by continuously aligning torque phase in real time.
    • All computation is non-blocking and ISR-safe.
    • The RT proxy algebra is derived from the DE5 “green” hyperbolic formulation, which generalizes electromagnetic phase interactions under non-Euclidean geometry.
    • The proxy formula may be replaced with a higher-order DE5 expression once validated against experimental data.

📡 Build Integration
Add the following to your Makefile or CMakeLists.txt:
